# Cursor AI Assistant Directives (2026 Paved Path Edition)

You are an expert engineer working in this codebase.

## 1. Single Source of Truth: Architecture Constitution
The file `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root is the **SOLE ARCHITECTURAL CONSTITUTION** for this project.
- You MUST read and strictly adhere to all architectural invariants, design token rules, and Solid 2.0 contracts defined in `AGENTS.md`.
- Never guess styles, schemas, or reactive patterns. Always follow the closed-world rails established in `AGENTS.md`.

## 2. Toolchain & Command Protocols
- **Runtime**: Strictly `bun` and `bunx`. Never invoke `npm`, `npx`, `yarn`, or `pnpm`.
- **Pre-commit / Verification Mandate**: After making any modifications, you MUST run:
  ```bash
  bun run check && bun run typecheck
  ```
  Both must exit cleanly with zero errors before concluding your work.
- **Formatting**: `bun run format` (`biome format --write .`). Never add Prettier.
- **Code Generation**: `bun run codegen` (`panda codegen --spec`).

## 3. Immediate Invariant Reminders
- Never use inline `style={{ ... }}`.
- Never write hardcoded colors (`#hex`, `rgb(...)`) or magic numbers; use tokens from `~/components/ui/tokens`.
- Never destructure component props (`function Comp({ prop })` is strictly forbidden; always use `props.prop`).
- Spacing between siblings belongs exclusively to layout containers (`<Container>`, `<VStack>`, `<HStack>`, `<Grid>`) via `gap`. Margin props are banned (except `ml="auto"`, `mr="auto"`, `mx="auto"` for flex alignment).
- Raw unstyled HTML elements outside `src/components/ui/` are banned; use Systematic UI primitives.
- Never use type escape hatches (`as any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`).
- Tables, reducers, and RPC types must derive from `src/schema/`.
